<title>FRANCE: Euro-Council wants 18-year-old parliamentarians.</title>
<headline>Euro-Council wants 18-year-old parliamentarians.</headline>
<dateline>STRASBOURG, France 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Council of Europe's parliamentary assembly suggested on Friday that the minimum age for parliamentarians across the continent be reduced to 18 years.</p>
<p>Eighteen-year olds can be deputies in Albania, Belgium and Portugal, but the threshold is set at 21 in Britain, 23 in France and 30 in Turkey.</p>
<p>The parliamentary assembly of the Council, which safeguards democracy and human rights in its 40 member countries, rejected a proposal that the minimum age for voting in local elections be cut from 18 in most countries to 16 years.</p>
</text>
